{"point":{"id":"workspace","title":"Browser Workspace Ownership","rationale":"CanvasWorkspace owns canvas session lifetimes; each CanvasSession exposes separate subscriptions for document, presentation, selection, controls, geometry, and status. WorkspacePersistence translates committed changes into incremental records, while RecordStorage coalesces writes and retries ambiguous failures with the identical request. This explains how many open canvases share persistence without publishing every pointer movement.","sourcePaths":["src/features/mapping/MappingPage.tsx","src/features/mapping/workspace/canvasWorkspace.ts","src/features/mapping/workspace/canvasSession.ts","src/features/mapping/workspace/workspacePersistence.ts","src/features/mapping/workspace/recordStorage.ts","src/features/mapping/workspace/workspaceStorage.ts","src/features/mapping/workspace/workspaceStorage.worker.ts"],"relationships":[{"pointId":"canvas_commands","label":"creates session controllers and retains editing contexts","kind":"ownership"},{"pointId":"persistence","label":"sends versioned record batches through workspace HTTP","kind":"call"},{"pointId":"rendering","label":"mounts an editor for each canvas session","kind":"ownership"}]},"sources":[{"path":"src/features/mapping/MappingPage.tsx","text":"import { extractLayoutTemplate, type LayoutCapture } from '../../../domain/core/diagrams/layoutTemplate';
